@startuml ShareKampus_UserFlow
title ShareKampus — User Flow (Campus Circular Loop)

|New Student|
start
:Open ShareKampus;
:Browse nearby item catalog\n(GET /items/nearby, no login required);

if (Interested in borrowing an item?) then (yes)
  :Register account\n(POST /auth/register)\n-- campus email domain validation --;
  :Login\n(POST /auth/login);
else (not yet, just browsing)
  stop
endif

|Borrower|
:Select the desired item;
:Submit a borrow/barter request\n(POST /transactions)\n-- status: pending --;
note right
  The item REMAINS visible as "available"
  to other students -- multiple pending
  requests can exist simultaneously
end note
:Wait for owner's approval;

|Item Owner|
:Receive the request notification;
if (Approve the borrower?) then (approve)
  :Approve\n(PATCH /transactions/:id/status\nstatus: active);
  :Item is automatically locked\n(items.status = on_transaction);
else (reject)
  :Reject\n(PATCH /transactions/:id/status\nstatus: rejected);
  stop
endif

|Borrower|
:Pick up the item from the owner\n(meet in person on campus);
:Use the item during the loan period;

|Borrower #LightYellow|
:Return the item;

fork
  |Borrower|
  :Mark as completed\n(PATCH /transactions/:id/status\nstatus: returned);
fork again
  |Item Owner|
  :Mark as completed\n(PATCH /transactions/:id/status\nstatus: returned);
end fork
note right
  Either party (borrower OR owner)
  may mark it as returned first
end note

:Item automatically becomes\navailable again\n(items.status = available);
:Both parties' Trust Score\nis automatically recalculated\n(recalculate_trust_score);

|Borrower|
:Leave a review for the owner\n(POST /reviews)\n-- rating 1-5 + comment --;
note right
  Only allowed once per transaction,
  and only for transactions with status returned
end note
:Owner's Trust Score\nis recalculated again\n(now including the average rating);

|Other Students|
:View the owner's profile before borrowing\n(GET /users/:id/trust-score)\n-- average rating, on-time ratio, etc. --;
:The same item can now be\nborrowed by the next student;
note right
  This is the "Campus Circular Loop" --
  a single item keeps circulating
  among many different students
end note

stop

@enduml